why Every Horde quest of Zul'Farrak in one run, lead-ins included.

# Zul'Farrak's Horde quests in one guide: the pick-ups in the Undercity, the
# Venom Bottles chain between the Hinterlands, Tarren Mill and Sen'jin
# Village, Mulgore, Dustwallow Marsh, Tanaris, the Shimmering Flats and
# Feralas (for Mages A Lesson in Literacy too), one run, then the hand-ins.
# Steps already done are passed over, so the guide picks up wherever the
# chain stands.
#
# The chains:
# - The Venom Bottles' 2933 -> Apothecary Lydon's 2934 Undamaged Venom Sac ->
#   2935 Consult Master Gadrin -> 2936 The Spider God (the Tablet of Theka
#   inside) -> 2937 Summoning Shadra.
# - Tabetha's Task 2861 (from Anastasia Hartwell) -> 2846 Tiara of the Deep.
# - Tran'rek's 2865 Scarab Shells; Trenton Lighthammer's 3042 Troll Temper;
#   Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle's 2768 Divino-matic Rod.
# - Yeh'kinya's 3520 Screecher Spirits -> 3527 The Prophecy of Mosh'aru ->
#   4787 The Ancient Egg.
# - Wizzle Brassbolts' 2770 Gahz'rilla.
# - Mazu'kon's 96775 Zum'rah's Head.
# - The OOX-17/TN Distress Beacon, a rare drop inside and in Tanaris, starts
#   351 Find OOX-17/TN! -> 648 Rescue OOX-17/TN! (an escort, then Booty Bay).
# - Mages: Owen Thadd's 82084 A Lesson in Literacy.
#
# Summoning Shadra comes last: Shadra is an elite of level 55, so that step
# waits for 55.
#
# Left out: 2864 Tran'rek, the breadcrumb from Krazek in Booty Bay (off this
# guide's way; Scarab Shells opens without it); 2938 and on, after Summoning
# Shadra; 3528 The God Hakkar after The Ancient Egg (it needs the Sunken
# Temple, whose guide holds it); 3721 An OOX of Your Own (it needs the other
# two OOX chains); 8676 Wildmane the Elder (the Lunar Festival); the Rogues'
# 80411 The Talisman of Kazdor (not on the Codex page; its text asks for the
# job to be done alone, not in a group's run).
#
# Gahz'rilla comes only when someone rings the gong by the sacred pool with
# the Mallet of Zul'Farrak, and one mallet does it for the group. Qiaga the
# Keeper, an elite on top of the Altar of Zul, drops the Sacred Mallet; used
# at the altar at the very top of Jintha'Alor it becomes the Mallet. The guide
# is in the Hinterlands anyway, so the Sacred Mallet is an optional goal
# there. Gahz'rilla's scale is optional too, for a group without a mallet;
# Wizzle's hand-in comes once the quest is done.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses, Sergeant Bly, the graves or
# the Tablet of Theka inside, so their goals stand at the door (@38.7,20.1,
# Tanaris) with `group 5`. The bosses come in the order of the client's
# dungeon journal (Hydromancer Velratha, Gahz'rilla, Antu'sul, Theka the
# Martyr, Witch Doctor Zum'rah, Nekrum Gutchewer, Shadowpriest Sezz'ziz, Chief
# Ukorz Sandscalp), not of a recorded run. Every quest goal is counted by the
# quest log, so a group that takes them in another order still gets each step
# ticked.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon. The Tiara, the tablets, the scale, the head,
#   the shells and the Troll Temper are quest items there: they drop only
#   while their quest is held. Sergeant Bly carries the rod. The Undamaged
#   Venom Sac lasts 30 minutes, and the Witherbark Broodguards drop it one
#   time in ten.
# - The Mallet of Zul'Farrak: the Codex page's note on it (the gong, one
#   mallet per group, Qiaga, Jintha'Alor); the data has Qiaga, an elite of
#   level 50 at the Altar of Zul, drop the Sacred Mallet every time.
# - The door: QuestieDB's list of Forever's dungeons, as Polestar's Codex holds it
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - The dungeon's size, levels and bosses: the client's group finder and
#   dungeon journal, as Polestar's Codex page holds them (five players, levels
#   44 to 54).
# - Lint warns that the door is more than 50 yards from the beacon's droppers
#   outside (in Tanaris and beyond); the optional goal stays at the door for
#   the ones inside.
# INGAME: where inside do the Tablet of Theka, Sergeant Bly and the Shallow
#   Graves stand?

